CORE
main.sh
--resolve-dynamic-sites --cvc5
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^\[assertion\.1\] .* 0 = 1: SUCCESS$
^\[shell-unsupported\.1\] .* the parts of the action of trap for the holes of "rm -f /dev/shm/\.vigpg-"\* have no character .*: SUCCESS$
^\[assertion\.2\] .* 0 = 2: SUCCESS$
^\[shell-unsupported\.[0-9]+\] .* the parts of the action of trap for the holes of "rm -rf "\*"tmp\."\* have no character .*: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The specification of mktemp: a template's name has no blanks, so that
the first trap's action is a word; without a template, the name is in
$TMPDIR, which may have one. (With refined strings, the pattern */tmp.*
is not decided: the string solver treats such models as counterexamples
when its not-contains constraints do not converge.)
